- **Exclusion note:** this report is written as `.md.excluded` because **Cat Jam is an anonymous, time-limited *stealth* model with zero published first‑party benchmarks** for this exact ID. Per `RULES.md`, a findings file is self-excluded (never fabricated) when there are no verified benchmarks. Every structured catalog either leaves it unscored or provider‑unknown: Command Code lists **"Cat Jam — Free — 1M — not yet scored"**; OpenCode Data files it under provider **`unknown/cat-jam`** (usage/token ranking only, no capability row); Artificial Analysis exposes no `cat-jam` model page. What exists is anecdotal social commentary ("very fast", "built for agentic coding", "small-model feeling"), not a reproducible benchmark — so no scores can be asserted without fabricating them. The panel's prior raters in this folder overwhelmingly reached the same verdict (see `Claude_Haiku_5.5.md.excluded`, `Claude_Sonnet_4.5.md.excluded`, `GPT_5.md.excluded`, `GPT_6_Luna.md.excluded`, `GPT_5.6_Luna.md.excluded`, `Gemini_2.5_Flash.md.excluded`, `Grok_4.5.md.excluded`, `Laguna_S_2.1.md.excluded`).

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** Cat Jam (`cat-jam`)
- **Status:** **ANONYMOUS STEALTH MODEL — UNREVEALED.** Launched as a free, limited-time stealth route on OpenCode Zen (announced on OpenCode's own feed: "Cat Jam (stealth model) is now free in OpenCode — very fast — built for agentic coding — zero data retention"). Unlike the earlier `ox-alpha` stealth listing (later de-anonymized as Z.ai GLM-5.3-Flash), **Cat Jam's underlying lab/model has not been revealed** as of 2026-10-17, so there is no base model to attribute benchmarks to.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen keyless free tier (`stealth/cat-jam` / `opencode/cat-jam`); $0 in/out; 1M-token advertised window; zero data retention. No vendor model card, no HuggingFace checkpoint, no canonical OpenRouter listing.
- **Release / knowledge:** anonymous preview drop (Oct 2026); no knowledge cutoff disclosed — none can be, absent an identified base model.
- **Context window:** curated `meta.json` "128K total" is a `scaffolded: true` placeholder; third-party catalogs advertise 1M. Neither is a first-party verified spec.
- **Modalities:** curated `meta.json` "Text in/out" — placeholder; positioning implies a text reasoning/coding model. No verified modality sheet.
- **Pricing:** free limited-time stealth tier; no first-party paid rate exists.
- **Architecture:** none disclosed. Community tests describe it as fast and "small-model feeling" but this is subjective, not an architecture disclosure.

